## 4. DISK PARTITION CONFIGURATION

The virtual machine uses a 60 GB virtual hard disk with the MBR partitioning scheme.

| Partition | Type | Size | Purpose |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Partition 1 | Primary | 21,000 MB | Windows operating system |
| Partition 2 | Logical | 19,000 MB | Data storage |
| Partition 3 | Logical | 19,000 MB | Additional data storage |
| Remaining | Unallocated | Approximately 2,000 MB | Available space |

The two logical drives are intended to be created inside an extended partition.

**Note:** The partition layout must be verified against the final installed configuration. Windows 10 requires at least 32 GB of storage, so the proposed 21 GB operating-system partition must be increased before installation.

